meta {
  name: Refund Records (Detailed)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/refund-records?statuses=ORDER,APPOINTMENT,CANCELLED&dimension=all&page=1&limit=20
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  statuses: ORDER,APPOINTMENT,CANCELLED
  dimension: all
  page: 1
  limit: 20
  ~dateFrom: 2026-07-01
  ~dateTo: 2026-07-31
  ~branchId: {{branchId}}
  ~paymentMode: CASH
  ~search: john
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Paginated detailed Refund records for the active tab (`dimension` — same set as
  Billing, incl. `outsource`). Only orders with a REFUND entry; every row carries
  `refundAmount` (Σ of the order's refunds) + `cancelAmount`, plus the standard money
  fields. Each row also carries the order's `refundStatus`
  (`NONE | PARTIALLY_REFUNDED | FULLY_REFUNDED`), which the report folds into the
  Status column ("Refunded" / "Partially Refunded") instead of the misleading
  "Not Paid" a fully-refunded order's `paymentStatus` would otherwise show. For the
  item-level dimensions each row's figures are the sum of that order's
  allocated matching lines (refund allocated proportionally by net).
  `Σ records === refund-summary` for the same filters.
}
